## 4. VALIDATION GATES

### Gate 1: Backend Infrastructure (After Phase 1)
- ✅ GCS bucket accessible via signed URLs
- ✅ Database tables created with correct schema
- ✅ All 4 API endpoints return 200 status codes
- ✅ Test video can be uploaded and downloaded

**Validation Command**:
```bash
# Test upload flow
curl -X POST http://localhost:5173/api/get-upload-url -d '{"fileName":"test.mp4","contentType":"video/mp4"}'
# Upload to returned URL
# Verify in GCS console: https://console.cloud.google.com/storage/browser/sora-2-app-videos
```

### Gate 2: Services Layer (After Phase 2)
- ✅ `cloudStorageService.uploadVideo()` successfully uploads test video
- ✅ `cloudStorageService.loadVideo()` returns video blob
- ✅ `cloudStorageService.listScenes()` returns user's scenes
- ✅ `remixService.autoRemix()` calls remix API correctly

**Validation Method**: Browser console testing with sample data

### Gate 3: State Management (After Phase 3)
- ✅ Store can create new scene
- ✅ Store can remix existing scene
- ✅ Store maintains version history correctly
- ✅ Store persists data across page reloads (via database)

**Validation Method**: React DevTools - inspect Zustand state after each action

### Gate 4: UI Components (After Phase 4)
- ✅ All components render without errors
- ✅ VideoCanvas displays video correctly
- ✅ RemixHistoryStack shows version thumbnails
- ✅ PromptEditor enables editing and remixing
- ✅ TimelineView generates thumbnails
- ✅ Clicking timeline thumbnail seeks video

**Validation Method**: Visual inspection + interaction testing

### Gate 5: End-to-End Workflow (After Phase 6)
- ✅ Complete user journey: Create → Remix → Extend → Reload
- ✅ Videos persist across sessions
- ✅ No console errors or warnings
- ✅ Performance acceptable on desktop browsers

**Validation Method**: Full user acceptance testing

