## 5. FINAL VALIDATION CHECKLIST

### Functional Requirements
- [ ] User can access previously created scenes
- [ ] User can create new scene from prompt
- [ ] User can edit prompt and remix automatically
- [ ] Remix history appears as vertical stack
- [ ] User can click old versions to preview
- [ ] Timeline shows thumbnail filmstrip
- [ ] Clicking timeline thumbnail seeks video
- [ ] User can extend scene with frame continuity
- [ ] Planner mode works with toggle
- [ ] All videos stored in GCS
- [ ] Metadata stored in Postgres
- [ ] Videos persist across browser sessions

### Non-Functional Requirements
- [ ] No ugly UI (clean, professional design)
- [ ] No console errors in production build
- [ ] Fast initial load (<3s on fast connection)
- [ ] Responsive layout (works on 1280x720+ screens)
- [ ] Error messages are user-friendly
- [ ] Loading states provide feedback

### Technical Requirements
- [ ] Code follows existing patterns (Zustand, services, Edge Functions)
- [ ] TypeScript types are complete and correct
- [ ] No TypeScript errors (`npm run build` succeeds)
- [ ] ESLint passes (`npm run lint`)
- [ ] Git branch `scenebuilder-v2-rebuild` is clean
- [ ] PR description references this PRP

---

## 6. CONFIDENCE ASSESSMENT

### Confidence Score: 8/10

**Reasoning**:
- ✅ **Architecture is well-researched**: 3 comprehensive AI docs created with exact implementations
- ✅ **Backend setup is straightforward**: GCS + Vercel Postgres have clear documentation
- ✅ **Existing patterns are reusable**: Video generation, frame extraction, polling all work
- ✅ **UI design is simplified**: Vertical stack + timeline is standard video editor pattern
- ⚠️ **Potential risks**:
  - GCS signed URL generation in Edge Functions (may need Node.js runtime)
  - Timeline thumbnail generation performance (could be slow for long videos)
  - Remix API time limits (1 hour vs 24 hours uncertainty)

**Mitigation Strategies**:
- Test GCS signed URLs early (Phase 1, Gate 1)
- Implement lazy thumbnail loading with intersection observer
- Add both 1-hour and 24-hour expiration warnings
- Use Vercel Postgres connection pooling to avoid timeout issues

